# Milestone: M5
# Covers: cross-spec chain: cond watcher fires → body emits event → event
#         subscriber fires; at(x > threshold) body emits e!, at(e?) logs.
#         Tests that a rising-edge cond watcher can trigger event dispatch
#         as a downstream effect (spec cross-spec §2.2).
#
# defer-to: T59 (Event.new()) + M5-scratch-frame (cond eval + body dispatch)
#
# Reason:
#   The cond watcher (at x>threshold) requires scratch-frame condition
#   evaluation (invoke_condition_closure stub).  The body dispatch requires
#   spawn_body_coroutine (stub).  Event.new() requires T59 stdlib binding.
#   The composition of cond-watcher + event emit is a pure sequencing of two
#   already-implemented C-level paths: watcher_eval_dirty → spawn body coroutine
#   → body runs e! → urbi_event_emit_async → event subscriber fires.
#
# Activate when Event.new() + cond eval + body dispatch are wired.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var threshold = 5;
#   var e = Event.new();
#   var log = "";
#   at (threshold > 3) e!;
#   at (e?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "event";
#   Realm.threshold = 10;
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] 5
#   [00000001] nil
#   [00000002] ""
#   [00000003] nil
#   [00000004] nil
#   [00000005] 10
#   [00000006] "event"
